 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Serbia's president of fourteen years just conceded defeat. To whom?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "On Sunday night, Aleksandar Vučić said the Student List had won Serbia's snap election. Final counts were not in. By his projection, the students take one hundred thirty-five to one hundred forty of two hundred fifty seats. His own list gets about one hundred five."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "The Student List grew out of almost two years of protests. They began after a train station canopy collapsed in Novi Sad in twenty twenty-four, killing sixteen people. Protesters accuse the government of corruption. Al Jazeera reports the highest turnout in decades."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Vučić blamed independent media, and alleged interference by unnamed European countries and an American deep state. Reuters compares the result to Orbán's defeat in Hungary in April. Results are preliminary. A presidential vote is due by May twenty twenty-seven."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Vučić's party accept the final result? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
