 "upload": {
  "title": "Serbia's Vučić Concedes to Student Protesters #shorts",
  "description": "On the night of Sunday, October 25, 2026, Serbian President Aleksandar Vučić conceded defeat in the snap parliamentary election to the student-led Student List. Based on a sample of votes, he projected the Student List at 135 to 140 of 250 seats and his own list at about 105; final results are still pending. The movement grew out of almost two years of protests that began after the 2024 Novi Sad railway station canopy collapse, which killed 16 people. Vučić blamed independent media and alleged interference by unnamed European countries and an \"American deep state\". Reuters compared the result to Viktor Orbán's defeat in Hungary in April.\n\nSources:\nCNN: Serbia's leader concedes defeat to student-led movement in seismic political shift (Oct 25, 2026)\nAl Jazeera: Serbia's Vucic concedes election defeat to student-led movement (Oct 25, 2026)\nEuronews: Student List wins Serbian election as Vučić concedes defeat (Oct 25, 2026)\nABC News (Australia): Serbian president concedes defeat to student-led movement (Oct 26, 2026)\nReuters via Times of Israel: Serbia's Vucic concedes election defeat in historic win for student protest movement (Oct 2026)\n\n#geopolitics #Serbia #Vucic #Europe",
